WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:08.200
In May nineteen fifty-two, at King's College London, a photograph took sixty-two hours to expose.

2
00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.450
It showed a faint black X.

3
00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:19.775
Rosalind Franklin and her student, Raymond Gosling, had made it, and it became number fifty-one.

4
00:00:20.775 --> 00:00:26.125
Eight months later, a colleague showed it to James Watson without telling her.

5
00:00:27.125 --> 00:00:29.925
Watson wrote that his mouth fell open.

6
00:00:30.875 --> 00:00:32.950
The X meant a helix.

7
00:00:33.925 --> 00:00:38.400
That spring, he and Francis Crick published the shape of DNA.

8
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.250
Franklin died in nineteen fifty-eight.

9
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.200
She was thirty-seven.

10
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:52.175
In nineteen sixty-two, the Nobel Prize for the double helix went to three men.

11
00:00:53.175 --> 00:00:55.450
She never knew he had seen it.
